.TH GENESIS-GAMES 7 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-games \- Genesis's game world: the collection, the shelf, and the ARC funnel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Games are a world she plays, not a benchmark she is run through.
The collection (\fBworlds/play.py\fR, \fIGamePlay\fR) is every game
she can reach; the shelf is what she wants to play right now \(em a
weighted draw over appeal, not a syllabus. Unplayed games draw
curiosity, unfinished ones pull by the near-miss grip, and a game
that has beaten her many times goes on the shelf (set aside, never
deleted). A mastered game is \fBarchived\fR: it stays in the record
and can still be pulled by name, but it stops drawing her picks.
.SH FAMILIES
.TP
.B grid
Puzzle grids \(em infer the rule from training pairs, produce the
answer grid. Includes the ARC corpora tasks (below).
.TP
.B sorter / sequence / assembly / relations / quantities / classification
Her built-in games, each with its own agent.
.TP
.B system
Installed desktop games (e.g. pacman). Actions: \fBup\fR, \fBdown\fR,
\fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, \fBspace\fR.
.TP
.B arcagi
Local ARC-AGI-3 environments \(em the practice arcade.
.TP
.B arc_official
The official scorecard \(em one standing entry, the challenge itself.
.SH THE ARC FUNNEL
.PP
Two feeds land on the same shelf, leveled so the harder tiers pull
harder (\fIlevel\fR adds appeal; internal games sit at 1):
.TP
.B arc_* (level 2)
ARC-AGI-1 corpus tasks \(em \fI~/testing/ARC/data/{training,evaluation}\fR.
.TP
.B arc2_* (level 3)
ARC-AGI-2 corpus tasks \(em \fI~/testing/ARC-AGI-2/data/{...}\fR.
.TP
.B arcagi-* (level 4)
The interactive environments \(em local engines only, offline; no
remote API feed. Their \fIgame_id\fR names match the official
card's, so practice mastery and card mastery are one record.
.PP
\fBGENESIS_ARC_CORPUS\fR adds corpus roots (os.pathsep-separated);
each root's \fIdata/{training,evaluation}\fR layout is understood,
and a bare directory of task files works too. Corpus specs are thin
\(em a task's grids load only when she actually sits at it.
.SH THE OFFICIAL CHALLENGE
.PP
The card is the summit, not the starting line. It stands on the
shelf only after she has mastered at least one ARC-family game
(\fI_arc_unlocked\fR \(em any of arc_, arc2_, arcagi- at
mastery 1.0). A card opens once per window, gives every game a
single recorded try, and closes on the venue's clocks (idle and
expiry). A card closed inside its window leaves the shelf empty
until the window lapses. Taking the challenge is her choice, raised
by a play urge; inside the sitting she plays the card out.
.SH CONTROLS
.PP
Environment games run through the cabinet \(em a small X11 window
whose inputs are real key and pointer events:
.nf
  W/\(ua  ACTION1      S/\(da  ACTION2
  A/\(la  ACTION3      D/\(ra  ACTION4
  Space/F ACTION5      click  ACTION6 (at the clicked cell)
  Z       ACTION7 (undo)      RESET   its own control
.fi
.PP
A fumbled press or a click that misses the board is a lost move,
never a retried one \(em same as a human's hand.
.SH RECORDS
.TP
.I <data>/gameplay.json
Mastery, attempts, disproven rules and predictions, learned play
values \(em her persistent record.
.TP
.I <data>/arc/results.jsonl
One JSONL line per environment result: state, levels, steps,
level_steps, decision_sources, prior_learning, recovery_waits, and
\fIscorecard_id\fR when the try was official. The research record.
.TP
.I <data>/arc/recordings/
The SDK's per-step recordings of every env run.
.TP
.I notebooks/arc_research.ipynb
The research view over both \(em loads the results log and the
recordings.
.SH FILES
.PP
\fBpython/worlds/play.py\fR \(em the collection, shelf, attempts,
funnel, and card.\fBpython/worlds/arc.py\fR \(em the practice and
official adapters.\fBpython/worlds/arc_cabinet.py\fR \(em the window
and its controls.
